Dev Technical Guidance
This story is foundational and highly complex, demanding meticulous attention to detail and robust automation. The AI agent's role in autofixing and test generation is a cornerstone of this workflow.
- Dependency: This story depends on Story 1.1: Establish Project Repositories and Monorepo Structure for the monorepo foundation.
- AI Agent Integration: The AI agent for this story needs to be capable of interacting with Git commands, linting tools, test runners, and potentially code generation frameworks to perform autofixing and test writing. This will require sophisticated tooling and access.
- Git Hooks: lefthook is preferred for its speed and flexibility over traditional Git hooks. lint-staged integrates with it.
- Commit Standards: cz-git and Commitlint enforce Conventional Commits. The AI's autowriting must adhere to these.
- Linting/Formatting: Configure ESLint v9 with appropriate rules. Biome.js can provide integrated linting/formatting/compilation; consider how it complements or replaces parts of ESLint/Prettier. Pylint for Python.
- Testing: Ensure unit test runners (e.g., Jest/PyTest) are correctly integrated. The AI's test generation should produce high-quality, passing tests.
- Code Coverage: Codecov integration for reporting. The AI's test generation must target the specified coverage thresholds.
- Containerization: Leverage Docker for consistent environments. Define clear image naming and tagging conventions.
- CI/CD Orchestration: GitHub Actions workflows will orchestrate the entire pipeline. Ensure turbo.json is optimized for parallel task execution and caching.
- Deployment Targets: Vercel for frontend, chosen cloud provider (AWS/GCP) for backend. Supabase/Turso/Neon for databases (consider "database per service" principle from Architecture Document).
- Security: Ensure all API keys (e.g., for AI agent access, Docker Hub) are securely managed via secrets. Implement CODEOWNERS for production branch protection. Refer to "Security Best Practices" in the Architecture Document.
- Error Handling: The pipeline itself should provide clear feedback on failures. AI autofixing should reduce manual debugging.
